her a hand grenade.

255
00:09:21,462 --> 00:09:24,665
Thank you, Mister Zebub.
(group chuckles)

256
00:09:25,632 --> 00:09:27,602
Ah, lung cancer.

257
00:09:30,137 --> 00:09:31,438
You have fingers.

258
00:09:31,472 --> 00:09:32,773
I like that in a man.

259
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:37,077
Ah, the American Institute
of Psychical Researchiculating.

260
00:09:38,645 --> 00:09:39,812
Come on into my meat freezer,

261
00:09:39,845 --> 00:09:42,082
I'd like to show you
my research on beefalo.

262
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:45,352
Should never have bought
that cow dung sprayer.

263
00:09:45,385 --> 00:09:47,053
(Mike chuckles)

264
00:09:47,087 --> 00:09:48,655
So you've come back, eh?

265
00:09:48,688 --> 00:09:50,423
After seven years,
you've come back.

266
00:09:50,457 --> 00:09:51,825
No, it's not me.

267
00:09:51,858 --> 00:09:53,627
Time has little
meaning in Tibet.

268
00:09:53,660 --> 00:09:54,762
Neither does the
word, Tacorific.

269
00:09:54,795 --> 00:09:56,128
Did my call startle you?

270
00:09:56,162 --> 00:09:58,798
No, I've been expecting
it for seven years.

271
00:09:58,832 --> 00:10:00,133
Well, six and a half.

272
00:10:00,167 --> 00:10:02,102
All of your old students
return, don't they, Professor?

273
00:10:02,135 --> 00:10:03,737
All your ruddy friends
are coming over tonight.

274
00:10:03,770 --> 00:10:04,705
Even the ones you failed.

275
00:10:04,738 --> 00:10:06,507
Particularly
the ones I failed.

276
00:10:06,540 --> 00:10:07,807
They always want
to prove me wrong.

277
00:10:07,840 --> 00:10:10,677
- And I always am wrong.
- And now you.

278
00:10:10,710 --> 00:10:12,945
You want to startle me
and the entire world, eh?

279
00:10:12,978 --> 00:10:15,683
- And I might do just that.
- Boo! Ha ha.

280
00:10:16,717 --> 00:10:17,783
With your help...

281
00:10:17,817 --> 00:10:19,718
I can make
seamless panty hose.

282
00:10:19,752 --> 00:10:22,422
When you called me, I said
I would listen, not help.

283
00:10:22,455 --> 00:10:23,790
Well, he is a psychologist.

284
00:10:23,823 --> 00:10:26,727
As for this
spectacular idea of yours,

285
00:10:26,760 --> 00:10:28,995
it's nothing but Sunday
supplement nonsense.

286
00:10:29,028 --> 00:10:32,298
I mean to invade
the depths of the mind.

287
00:10:32,332 --> 00:10:33,700
That is not nonsense.

288
00:10:33,733 --> 00:10:35,368
Excuse me, did
I say, "nonsense"?

289
00:10:35,402 --> 00:10:36,470
I meant fluffer nutter.

290
00:10:36,503 --> 00:10:37,737
I mean idiocy.

291
00:10:37,770 --> 00:10:39,807
Don't condemn me
without a try, Professor.

292
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:41,073
Too late, you're condemned.

293
00:10:41,107 --> 00:10:44,010
If I succeed, we will
see history unfold itself

294
00:10:44,043 --> 00:10:46,480
through the eyes of the subject.

295
00:10:46,513 --> 00:10:48,082
And I know it can be done.

296
00:10:48,115 --> 00:10:49,548
I've seen it.

297
00:10:49,582 --> 00:10:51,418
In the desert huts of
the Shamans of Kassa.

298
00:10:51,452 --> 00:10:52,685
And in Des Moines.

299
00:10:52,718 --> 00:10:53,687
And where will you
find a subject weak

300
00:10:53,720 --> 00:10:54,855
and impressionable
enough to arrive

301
00:10:54,888 --> 00:10:56,490
in the required depth of trance?

302
00:10:56,523 --> 00:10:58,892
- They're around.
- Diana...

303
00:10:58,925 --> 00:11:02,662
I'm recombining
DNA, if you don't mind.

304
00:11:02,695 --> 00:11:04,598
What's her full name?
(Servo imitates creaking)

305
00:11:04,632 --> 00:11:05,798
Who knows?

306
00:11:05,832 --> 00:11:08,002
She calls herself Diana Love.

307
00:11:08,035 --> 00:11:09,802
But her real
name is Dynamite.

308
00:11:09,835 --> 00:11:12,205
Don't be afraid, my dear,
no one's going to hurt you.

309
00:11:12,238 --> 00:11:14,808
I'm not afraid of
you, or anybody else.

310
00:11:14,842 --> 00:11:16,677
We'll be with you
in a moment, Diana.

311
00:11:16,710 --> 00:11:17,677
Where did you find her?

312
00:11:17,710 --> 00:11:19,445
What does it matter?

313
00:11:19,478 --> 00:11:21,113
You took her off
the street tonight?

314
00:11:21,147 --> 00:11:23,717
(Servo sings nonchalantly)
You unmitigated fool.

315
00:11:23,750 --> 00:11:25,152
- Am I?
- Ah, his blush.

316
00:11:25,185 --> 00:11:26,753
Her type is the
most easily influenced

317
00:11:26,787 --> 00:11:28,422
in basic character groups.

318
00:11:28,455 --> 00:11:29,890
Almost devoid of willpower.

319
00:11:29,923 --> 00:11:32,325
That's why I chose
one of her class.

320
00:11:32,358 --> 00:11:33,460
Has she agreed to this?

321
00:11:33,493 --> 00:11:35,262
I'm paying her well,

322
00:11:35,295 --> 00:11:38,698
although I dare say she has no
idea what I'm paying her for.

323
00:11:38,732 --> 00:11:40,033
I will not help you, Quintus.

324
00:11:40,067 --> 00:11:42,135
Then I'll do it
alone, without your help.

325
00:11:42,168 --> 00:11:44,270
Don't you want to
protect her, Professor?

326
00:11:44,303 --> 00:11:46,807
- Don't you have any Proust?
- From me?

327
00:11:48,242 --> 00:11:49,343
It'll take too long.

328
00:11:50,210 --> 00:11:52,012
Weeks.
48 hours.

329
00:11:52,045 --> 00:11:53,047
Impossible.

330
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:54,680
Instead of repeated sessions,

331
00:11:54,713 --> 00:11:57,083
I'll keep her under
the full two days.

332
00:11:57,117 --> 00:11:59,118
I won't even wake her up to eat.

333
00:11:59,152 --> 00:12:02,055
Instead, I'll direct all
her needs within the trance.

334
00:12:02,088 --> 00:12:04,157
- That could prove fatal.
- Why thank you.

335
00:12:04,190 --> 00:12:07,760
No, not with you
watching, Doctor.

336
00:12:07,793 --> 00:12:10,063
I see I have no
choice in the matter.

337
00:12:10,097 --> 00:12:11,698
A scientist with
a deep knife scar.

338
00:12:11,732 --> 00:12:12,933
We'll be remembered for this.

339
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:15,868
I hope it will
not be as murderers.

340
00:12:15,902 --> 00:12:18,038
Oh, you can kill me,
that's okay, I don't care.

341
00:12:20,007 --> 00:12:21,140
Say, how much
longer am I gonna

342
00:12:21,173 --> 00:12:23,377
have to stay in
this crummy joint?

343
00:12:23,410 --> 00:12:26,380
Two days, perhaps longer.

344
00:12:26,413 --> 00:12:27,515
Two years later...

345
00:12:28,415 --> 00:12:29,617
Do you have to do all that?

346
00:12:29,650 --> 00:12:31,017
Take it easy, Diana.

347
00:12:31,050 --> 00:12:32,518
Don't let the sound of your
own wheels drive you crazy.

348
00:12:32,552 --> 00:12:34,287
Are you subject
to fainting spells?

349
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:35,988
Hey, he has a Ben
Franklin ice auger.

350
00:12:36,022 --> 00:12:38,190
Do you have any difficulty
getting up in the morning?

351
00:12:38,223 --> 00:12:39,727
(Crow moans and grunts)
(Diana chuckles)

352
00:12:39,760 --> 00:12:40,460
I don't.

353
00:12:41,528 --> 00:12:43,130
- I get up in the afternoon.
- Felix.

354
00:12:44,163 --> 00:12:45,332
That's easy.

355
00:12:45,365 --> 00:12:46,098
I think you'll live.

356
00:12:46,132 --> 00:12:48,435
Unless loser here, kills you.

357
00:12:51,205 --> 00:12:52,773
Your witness.

358
00:12:53,807 --> 00:12:56,810
Dirty, greasy walls,
a short-lived design fad.

359
00:12:56,843 --> 00:12:59,680
I don't think I
wanna be hypnotized.

360
00:12:59,713 --> 00:13:01,615
You're being paid $500.

361
00:13:01,648 --> 00:13:02,782
That's a lot
of money back now.

362
00:13:02,815 --> 00:13:03,783
I think it might
be better if you

363
00:13:03,817 --> 00:13:06,153
took off that heavy bracelet.

364
00:13:06,187 --> 00:13:07,220
No, thanks.

365
00:13:07,253 --> 00:13:09,423
I'll just keep it,
if you don't mind.

366
00:13:09,457 --> 00:13:10,790
Very well.

367
00:13:10,823 --> 00:13:13,127
Say, friend, tell her a
penny saved is a penny earned.

368
00:13:14,862 --> 00:13:16,363
Do you see my hand?

369
00:13:16,397 --> 00:13:17,997
Do you think I'm Dale?

370
00:13:18,030 --> 00:13:20,833
There is no end
to my hand, is there?

371
00:13:20,867 --> 00:13:22,802
No, I guess I'm
not getting it, sorry.

372
00:13:22,835 --> 00:13:24,872
You can always
take another turn.

373
00:13:24,905 --> 00:13:27,173
Oh, and by the way, sleep!

374
00:13:29,075 --> 00:13:30,477
Around the knuckle...

375
00:13:30,510 --> 00:13:31,745
Over the gums.

376
00:13:31,778 --> 00:13:32,878
Over the finger.

377
00:13:32,912 --> 00:13:34,280
Look out, stomach,
here it comes.

378
00:13:34,313 --> 00:13:36,348
Like riding a tiny
roller coaster, isn't it?

379
00:13:36,382 --> 00:13:38,852
In that I feel like
throwing up on you?

380
00:13:38,885 --> 00:13:40,420
- Yes...
- Yes.

381
00:13:41,087 --> 00:13:42,655
Yes, yes.
You're riding.

382
00:13:42,688 --> 00:13:44,123
- And now, sleep!
- Whoa!

383
00:13:45,492 --> 00:13:46,427
First slowly...

384
00:13:46,460 --> 00:13:47,895
Then fastly.

385
00:13:49,095 --> 00:13:50,230
- Then faster.
- Give me liberty,

386
00:13:50,263 --> 00:13:53,667
or give me, oh no
wait, that's Pat Henry.

387
00:13:53,700 --> 00:13:55,035
Around...

388
00:13:55,068 --> 00:13:57,470
- Do you like my lip liner?
- Around,

389
00:13:58,738 --> 00:13:59,840
and around.

390
00:13:59,873 --> 00:14:00,973
He's not hypnotizing her,

391
00:14:01,007 --> 00:14:02,943
- he's merely boring her.
- Silent.

392
00:14:04,610 --> 00:14:07,680
- Silent.
- He's hypnotized himself.

393
00:14:07,713 --> 00:14:08,415
Silent.

394
00:14:09,348 --> 00:14:11,852
(group imitates spooky music)

395
00:14:11,885 --> 00:14:13,787
Five years later...
(group chuckles)

396
00:14:13,820 --> 00:14:16,723
And the silence is
deeper, and deeper.

397
00:14:16,757 --> 00:14:18,792
(group imitates spooky music)

398
00:14:18,825 --> 00:14:19,993
Like a well.

399
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:23,563
Like a deep, deep well.

400
00:14:23,597 --> 00:14:24,865
Like a circle in a spiral.

401
00:14:24,898 --> 00:14:25,798
Like falling.

402
00:14:25,832 --> 00:14:27,567
Like a wheel within a wheel.

403
00:14:27,600 --> 00:14:28,602
Falling...

404
00:14:29,768 --> 00:14:31,738
- Into a deep...
- Cleansing.

405
00:14:31,772 --> 00:14:32,938
- Discount.
- Deep...

406
00:14:32,972 --> 00:14:34,207
- Heating.
- Purple!

407
00:14:34,240 --> 00:14:36,910
Sleep.
(group imitates snoring)

408
00:14:36,943 --> 00:14:40,915
We are in a dark silence,
and we breathe in water.

409
00:14:42,248 --> 00:14:43,215
We are one.

410
00:14:43,248 --> 00:14:44,517
You know, early
to bed, early to rise

411
00:14:44,550 --> 00:14:47,955
makes a man healthy,
wealthy and wise, no?

412
00:14:49,022 --> 00:14:51,592
- When I touch you...
- I think about myself.

413
00:14:51,625 --> 00:14:53,260
No, no, no, wait, that's wrong.

414
00:14:53,293 --> 00:14:54,160
We will be one.

415
00:14:54,193 --> 00:14:55,828
We'll be me, for
convenience sake.

416
00:14:55,862 --> 00:15:00,935
(Mystery Science Theater
3000 theme music)

417
00:15:03,570 --> 00:15:05,172
You're going back farther.

418
00:15:06,873 --> 00:15:08,073
Going back...

419
00:15:08,107 --> 00:15:10,978
Back, back, oh, I snagged
it on the warning track!

420
00:15:12,478 --> 00:15:13,980
It is another time.

421
00:15:14,813 --> 00:15:18,318
Must not look at
Mister Weatherbee.

422
00:15:19,652 --> 00:15:22,522
- Farther...
- I’ve always loathed pencils.

423
00:15:24,857 --> 00:15:25,992
And when you wake up, I'll be

424
00:15:26,025 --> 00:15:27,893
the foxiest guy
you've ever seen.

425
00:15:27,927 --> 00:15:28,795
What are you doing?

426
00:15:28,828 --> 00:15:29,997
She can't possibly hear you.

427
00:15:31,363 --> 00:15:32,598
Can we roll her
out in the hall?

428
00:15:32,632 --> 00:15:34,133
I've got other clients.

429
00:15:35,402 --> 00:15:39,338
No, I am nowhere.

430
00:15:39,372 --> 00:15:40,507
Oh, Nebraska.

431
00:15:41,540 --> 00:15:44,510
- But I exist.
- My glasses popped on!

432
00:15:44,543 --> 00:15:48,048
You may speak.
(Crow imitates barking)

433
00:15:48,082 --> 00:15:49,282
Do you hear me?

434
00:15:51,185 --> 00:15:52,118
Oui.

435
00:15:52,152 --> 00:15:54,788
Are family, I've
got all my sis...

436
00:15:54,822 --> 00:15:56,155
What do you see?

437
00:15:56,188 --> 00:15:57,757
(Diana speaks French)

438
00:15:57,790 --> 00:16:01,293
Tish! That's French!
(imitates kissing)

439
00:16:01,327 --> 00:16:03,963
I will no longer
shower or shave my legs.

440
00:16:05,165 --> 00:16:07,300
And I hate all Americans now.

441
00:16:09,937 --> 00:16:12,272
Well, it's happened.

442
00:16:12,305 --> 00:16:14,540
Something about a
hat, that's all I got.

443
00:16:14,573 --> 00:16:16,610
You've broken into the past.

444
00:16:16,643 --> 00:16:17,712
Yes.

445
00:16:18,812 --> 00:16:20,280
Yes, I have.

446
00:16:21,882 --> 00:16:23,583
Yes, it's the 23rd
hour of our telethon,

447
00:16:23,617 --> 00:16:24,985
and we're going all the way.

448
00:16:25,852 --> 00:16:27,787
Now the real work will begin.

449
00:16:27,820 --> 00:16:29,055
What more is there to do?

450
00:16:29,088 --> 00:16:31,157
Well, the wall,
for one thing.

451
00:16:31,190 --> 00:16:33,360
So you were French once.

452
00:16:33,393 --> 00:16:34,562
And of nobility.

453
00:16:36,095 --> 00:16:38,230
You see it all too
dimly, don't you, Diana?

454
00:16:38,263 --> 00:16:39,800
Yes, through a
glass darkly, yeah.

455
00:16:39,833 --> 00:16:41,135
Too dimly.

456
00:16:42,102 --> 00:16:44,237
- Well, my dear...
- I don't give a damn.

457
00:16:44,270 --> 00:16:47,373
You will find that
there are other times,

458
00:16:47,407 --> 00:16:48,608
and other lives.

459
00:16:50,175 --> 00:16:52,645
Soon you will find
one that I may visit.

460
00:16:52,678 --> 00:16:54,447
Although I have been
barred from most times

461
00:16:54,480 --> 00:16:56,750
'cause of my unpaid
parking tickets.

462
00:16:56,783 --> 00:16:58,117
Come on, open
the hangar door...

463
00:16:58,150 --> 00:16:59,418
(imitates airplane engine)
That's a good girl.

464
00:16:59,452 --> 00:17:01,120
Research has
shown that my lap

465
00:17:01,153 --> 00:17:03,090
is the best place for her.

466
00:17:04,923 --> 00:17:08,162
I, I have no
heartbeat, oh, my G...

467
00:17:10,530 --> 00:17:13,600
She's all the way back
to Quest For Fire time.

468
00:17:13,633 --> 00:17:17,037
(grunts)

469
00:17:18,203 --> 00:17:19,372
Oh, why do I do this?

470
00:17:19,405 --> 00:17:22,075
I hypnotize all day,
then I go home to a cat.

471
00:17:23,542 --> 00:17:25,912
It's Must See TV
night, I have to get home!

472
00:17:25,945 --> 00:17:27,313
You told her nothing?

473
00:17:27,913 --> 00:17:29,615
You asked her nothing?

474
00:17:29,648 --> 00:17:30,817
Watch carefully.

475
00:17:30,850 --> 00:17:33,853
Your watching's been
pretty lax, these days.

476
00:17:33,887 --> 00:17:35,055
It's started.

477
00:17:35,755 --> 00:17:36,857
She's going.

478
00:17:36,890 --> 00:17:38,892
Oh, I'm puffy, I'm so puffy.

479
00:17:38,925 --> 00:17:41,160
I'm retaining
water in my wrists.

480
00:17:41,193 --> 00:17:42,695
Why'd you bring
her sewing kit?

481
00:17:42,728 --> 00:17:46,300
Dinosaur is trying to
take my charm bracelet, I...

482
00:17:50,003 --> 00:17:52,572
Slightly Risky Liasons.

483
00:17:52,605 --> 00:17:55,375
She's in the gorilla exhibit
at the Lincoln Park Zoo.

484
00:17:56,708 --> 00:17:58,610
- Sir Ray Nitschke.
- Ew.

485
00:17:58,643 --> 00:18:01,782
- How fares the witch?
- Real, real nice, thanks.

486
00:18:01,815 --> 00:18:04,250
Do you fear me, Sorceress?

487
00:18:04,283 --> 00:18:05,952
Why, Gobbo's the gentlest jailer

488
00:18:05,985 --> 00:18:07,820
ever to gouge a prisoner's eye.

489
00:18:07,853 --> 00:18:09,388
You wanna run
that by me again?

490
00:18:11,057 --> 00:18:12,558
Keep thee from me!

491
00:18:12,592 --> 00:18:13,960
Fret me not, hell hag.

492
00:18:13,993 --> 00:18:15,127
Miss Hell Hag.

493
00:18:15,160 --> 00:18:16,395
You've lost your
powers as tomorrow

494
00:18:16,428 --> 00:18:17,897
you shall lose your head
upon the chopping block!

495
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:19,798
- Chubby block?
- My head?

496
00:18:19,832 --> 00:18:21,033
I shall lose my head?

497
00:18:21,067 --> 00:18:22,602
Uh, you're
singing your hair...

498
00:18:22,635 --> 00:18:23,770
(group chuckles)

499
00:18:23,803 --> 00:18:25,772
Has your brain recoiled
from it and forgotten?

500
00:18:25,805 --> 00:18:26,873
Aye, you shall lose it,

501
00:18:26,907 --> 00:18:28,573
and it will roll like a melon,

502
00:18:28,607 --> 00:18:29,875
and you'll be clutching
it to your bosom

503
00:18:29,908 --> 00:18:31,577
when they bury you
at the crossroads,

504
00:18:31,610 --> 00:18:33,880
a stake through
your black heart.

505
00:18:33,913 --> 00:18:35,615
- Ew!
- Yes, I remember.

506
00:18:36,348 --> 00:18:37,417
They said I was a witch.

507
00:18:37,450 --> 00:18:38,785
She has a
Flashdance look going.

508
00:18:38,818 --> 00:18:39,952
- Yeah.
- But it's a lie,

509
00:18:39,985 --> 00:18:41,087
a terrible lie,
I am not a witch.

510
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:42,022
You must believe me!

511
00:18:42,055 --> 00:18:43,290
But I believe it!

512
00:18:44,057 --> 00:18:45,157
Look on me.

513
00:18:45,190 --> 00:18:46,192
He's an attractive
prison matron.

514
00:18:46,225 --> 00:18:47,727
Am I not ugly?

515
00:18:47,760 --> 00:18:50,563
Am I not the rancid
bed of a fetid swamp?

516
00:18:50,597 --> 00:18:51,697
