767
00:28:08,853 --> 00:28:10,857
If I found no
other course, yes.

768
00:28:10,890 --> 00:28:12,825
Wouldst thou
eatest a jar of bugs?

769
00:28:12,858 --> 00:28:15,727
Wouldst that I had a
love as great as thine.

770
00:28:15,760 --> 00:28:17,095
What arts thou
supported with, Livia?

771
00:28:17,128 --> 00:28:18,630
Where do you
journey, this night?

772
00:28:18,663 --> 00:28:19,465
To the cemetery.

773
00:28:20,567 --> 00:28:22,202
I must speak with
the digger Smolkin.

774
00:28:22,235 --> 00:28:23,202
Slab-o-face.

775
00:28:23,235 --> 00:28:25,772
They convicted Helene
of bewitching him.

776
00:28:25,805 --> 00:28:28,340
- I believe it not.
- Nor I.

777
00:28:28,373 --> 00:28:32,077
Go, seek poor Smolkin and bring
the proof to free thy love.

778
00:28:32,110 --> 00:28:33,412
Thank you, Livia.

779
00:28:33,445 --> 00:28:34,747
Good night.

780
00:28:34,780 --> 00:28:37,550
Take care, 'tis the eve
of the witch's Sabbath.

781
00:28:37,583 --> 00:28:39,818
So, fare thee well and stuff.

782
00:28:42,922 --> 00:28:43,822
Oh!

783
00:28:43,855 --> 00:28:45,458
Ow, that one hurt
for some reason.

784
00:28:47,827 --> 00:28:48,793
- His nose grew!
- The needle

785
00:28:48,827 --> 00:28:50,862
of my compass swings to north.

786
00:28:50,895 --> 00:28:53,732
'Tis whimpering Helene I put
in prison for the axe to kiss.

787
00:28:53,765 --> 00:28:55,233
Yeah, kiss my axe.

788
00:28:55,267 --> 00:28:57,303
Next, we'll meet
Pendragon at his tavern home.

789
00:28:58,703 --> 00:29:00,873
'Ere this night is done,
I'll have his heart,

790
00:29:00,907 --> 00:29:03,642
or else I'll have his soul.

791
00:29:03,675 --> 00:29:05,978
I feel delighted
in a generic way.

792
00:29:07,012 --> 00:29:09,013
Ah, Weekend at
Bernies, the early years.

793
00:29:09,047 --> 00:29:11,283
This is how Anthony
Quinn's wife must feel.

794
00:29:11,317 --> 00:29:12,518
(group chuckles)

795
00:29:14,053 --> 00:29:15,922
Ah, the medieval Squiggy.

796
00:29:15,955 --> 00:29:17,723
Let's see, what
rhymes with coffin?

797
00:29:17,757 --> 00:29:20,192
Hoffin, Soften,
John McLaughlin...

798
00:29:20,225 --> 00:29:22,862
He also does puppet
shows with the corpses.

799
00:29:24,730 --> 00:29:25,765
Arthur's keeper,

800
00:29:26,832 --> 00:29:30,002
I would have a room for
my mouldering friend.

801
00:29:30,035 --> 00:29:31,970
Are you the digger Smolkin?

802
00:29:32,003 --> 00:29:34,172
I've been told
that I am Smolkin,

803
00:29:34,205 --> 00:29:37,008
but I am mad so cannot
be sure of anything.

804
00:29:37,042 --> 00:29:38,545
Then how can you
be sure you're mad?

805
00:29:39,712 --> 00:29:40,845
You are bewitched?

806
00:29:40,878 --> 00:29:42,715
- Terribly.
- Bothered? Bewildered?

807
00:29:42,748 --> 00:29:45,550
Well tell me,
Smolkin, I must know.

808
00:29:45,583 --> 00:29:47,185
Was it Helene who did it to you?

809
00:29:47,218 --> 00:29:50,688
Helene, who must suffer
death for thy enchantment?

810
00:29:50,722 --> 00:29:53,692
Being enchanted, I
have no way of knowing.

811
00:29:53,725 --> 00:29:56,095
They say the enchantment
has destroyed my reason.

812
00:29:56,128 --> 00:29:57,430
- That's a face.
- Without reason,

813
00:29:57,463 --> 00:29:58,997
there is no memory.

814
00:29:59,030 --> 00:30:01,567
So it must follow
that I do not remember

815
00:30:01,600 --> 00:30:03,568
who it was who bewitched me.

816
00:30:03,602 --> 00:30:05,503
Do you jest with
me, grave digger?

817
00:30:05,537 --> 00:30:07,038
Again, I cannot say.

818
00:30:07,072 --> 00:30:11,143
I am mad, so therefore cannot
tell a jest from a joust.

819
00:30:11,177 --> 00:30:12,978
Dig's graves and
plays with your mind.

820
00:30:13,012 --> 00:30:14,580
I have much to do this night.

821
00:30:14,613 --> 00:30:15,980
Gotta help
Strider move a couch.

822
00:30:16,013 --> 00:30:18,617
I don't think thou
art as mad as all say.

823
00:30:18,650 --> 00:30:19,918
Come on, Huggie,
what do you know?

824
00:30:19,952 --> 00:30:21,453
Stir up thy brain, Smolkin.

825
00:30:22,755 --> 00:30:25,223
I'll be back to ask more of you.

826
00:30:25,257 --> 00:30:27,593
Again, I cannot say
if you will be back

827
00:30:27,627 --> 00:30:28,827
for I am mad.

828
00:30:28,860 --> 00:30:31,330
And wouldst thou pick
me up a MAD Magazine?

829
00:30:31,363 --> 00:30:34,633
I have to watch
Mad About You tonight.

830
00:30:34,667 --> 00:30:36,568
Madness is just
a cry for help.

831
00:30:36,602 --> 00:30:39,605
Ah, well, back to work.

832
00:30:39,638 --> 00:30:41,507
And back to my
Tin Pan Alley songs.

833
00:30:41,540 --> 00:30:43,008
♪ Dickety, dickety horse

834
00:30:43,042 --> 00:30:45,977
- Oh, cripes.
- ♪ My guest is dead, of course

835
00:30:46,010 --> 00:30:49,280
- ♪ The clock struck two
- Central time.

836
00:30:49,313 --> 00:30:53,418
- ♪ He's turning blue
- And I'm Hindu Babaloo,

837
00:30:53,452 --> 00:30:55,988
Dippity do, yadda, hoona, hey.
(Servo laughs)

838
00:30:56,022 --> 00:30:58,690
♪ With little or no remorse

839
00:30:58,723 --> 00:30:59,892
Oh, that was pretty weak.

840
00:30:59,925 --> 00:31:01,127
Yeah, it didn't
quite scan, did it?

841
00:31:01,160 --> 00:31:04,228
(Helene cries)
(bangs on coffin)

842
00:31:04,262 --> 00:31:06,498
Hey, something actually
stopped him from singing.

843
00:31:06,532 --> 00:31:07,433
Yay!

844
00:31:07,967 --> 00:31:09,100
Nice.

845
00:31:09,133 --> 00:31:11,603
Apparently there were Hardware
Hanks in the middle ages.

846
00:31:11,637 --> 00:31:14,807
Gettest thou a cemetery
full of savings, at Menards!

847
00:31:14,840 --> 00:31:16,908
(Helene cries out)

848
00:31:16,942 --> 00:31:19,045
Uh, you could help me
from the inside, you know.

849
00:31:20,112 --> 00:31:23,248
(Helene gasps)
Soft, girl, soft.

850
00:31:23,282 --> 00:31:25,283
- I’ll say.
- Thou art safe.

851
00:31:25,317 --> 00:31:28,887
What grisly monster
closed you in this box?

852
00:31:28,920 --> 00:31:30,755
- Whoa, don't do that!
- Was it I?

853
00:31:30,788 --> 00:31:32,825
Help me, for
God's sake, help me.

854
00:31:32,858 --> 00:31:34,727
Aye, that I will,
though my entangled brain

855
00:31:34,760 --> 00:31:36,997
could bring thee
more harm than help.

856
00:31:37,830 --> 00:31:38,963
Do I know thee?

857
00:31:38,997 --> 00:31:40,532
Weren't we in
homeroom together?

858
00:31:40,565 --> 00:31:41,767
Yes, yes, I do.

859
00:31:41,800 --> 00:31:44,837
Thou art Helene, who
cast a spell on me!

860
00:31:44,870 --> 00:31:47,238
Spell?
Nay, not I.

861
00:31:47,272 --> 00:31:49,875
If you are Smolkin then you know
we have never met before.

862
00:31:49,908 --> 00:31:52,010
If I am Smolkin.

863
00:31:52,043 --> 00:31:53,445
I may be James Coco.

864
00:31:53,478 --> 00:31:56,048
- Come, out of this rot.
- And into my rot.

865
00:31:56,082 --> 00:31:57,983
And tell me what I may do.

866
00:31:58,017 --> 00:31:59,718
Anyone gonna bury
me some time soon?

867
00:31:59,752 --> 00:32:00,953
Oh, I beg you.

868
00:32:01,420 --> 00:32:02,553
Hide me, please.

869
00:32:02,587 --> 00:32:05,123
Get me to a place that
I may stay the night.

870
00:32:05,157 --> 00:32:07,827
At 12 the witch's
Sabbath will occur.

871
00:32:07,860 --> 00:32:09,395
At dawn, they will execute

872
00:32:09,428 --> 00:32:11,563
the three witches
condemned by law.

873
00:32:11,597 --> 00:32:13,632
Oh, if I may but live
to see the sunrise,

874
00:32:13,665 --> 00:32:16,102
I shall have a whole year
to prove my innocence.

875
00:32:16,135 --> 00:32:17,737
These laws are
positively medieval.

876
00:32:17,770 --> 00:32:18,903
Aye, the witch's Sabbath.

877
00:32:18,937 --> 00:32:20,940
It will be held this
very night, here,

878
00:32:20,973 --> 00:32:23,608
in mine own cherished cemetery.

879
00:32:23,642 --> 00:32:25,577
Go, into the mutton cart.

880
00:32:25,610 --> 00:32:26,778
I'll take thee to a place

881
00:32:26,812 --> 00:32:29,815
where none save Satan
himself might find thee.

882
00:32:29,848 --> 00:32:31,650
His head looks
like a sand trap.

883
00:32:31,683 --> 00:32:33,352
Lie still, old man.

884
00:32:34,185 --> 00:32:36,088
I'll make thy bed when I return.

885
00:32:36,122 --> 00:32:37,757
And I'll leave
a light on for you.

886
00:32:37,790 --> 00:32:40,025
(Servo hums)
(cat meows)

887
00:32:41,627 --> 00:32:42,628
Meow.

888
00:32:43,695 --> 00:32:44,897
Me, wow.

889
00:32:44,930 --> 00:32:46,532
Ah, she still coughs
up hairballs, though.

890
00:32:46,565 --> 00:32:48,902
I'd like to flea bomb
her, I'll tell you that.

891
00:32:48,935 --> 00:32:50,168
Hey, hey.

892
00:32:51,770 --> 00:32:52,938
Hey, she's got a zipper.

893
00:32:52,972 --> 00:32:54,238
Weren't those invented--

894
00:32:54,272 --> 00:32:56,642
If she wants a zipper,
she can have a zipper, Mike.

895
00:32:56,675 --> 00:32:58,143
- Ow!
- Hee hee.

896
00:32:59,678 --> 00:33:00,480
Good evening, Livia.

897
00:33:01,413 --> 00:33:02,748
Welcome to the Gabriel's Horn.

898
00:33:02,782 --> 00:33:03,915
- Sorry, we're full.
- Join me,

899
00:33:03,948 --> 00:33:05,250
Scroop, and rest
thy meaty burden.

900
00:33:05,283 --> 00:33:06,952
All staff'll
be down in a sec.

901
00:33:06,985 --> 00:33:08,253
I see you are prepared.

902
00:33:08,287 --> 00:33:11,690
Corn flowers, wolfsbane,
chicken bones.

903
00:33:11,723 --> 00:33:13,592
Snakes, frogs and amulets.

904
00:33:13,625 --> 00:33:14,827
Big screen TV.

905
00:33:14,860 --> 00:33:17,162
No witch will pass
my door, this night.

906
00:33:17,195 --> 00:33:19,865
And here's garlic,
best protection of all.

907
00:33:19,898 --> 00:33:21,467
Hate it when the
waiter sits down with you.

908
00:33:21,500 --> 00:33:22,867
If there's one who
can handle witches

909
00:33:22,900 --> 00:33:24,770
- and the imps that serve them,
- Oh, boy.

910
00:33:24,803 --> 00:33:26,772
It's Scroop of
the Gabriel's Horn.

911
00:33:26,805 --> 00:33:27,940
We can't all be clever.

912
00:33:27,973 --> 00:33:29,107
And don't feed your
imp from the table,

913
00:33:29,140 --> 00:33:30,542
he won't go back to
his regular food.

914
00:33:30,575 --> 00:33:32,845
- Scroop, bring some ale.
- Rest thy corpulence.

915
00:33:32,878 --> 00:33:33,978
I'll take the ale.

916
00:33:34,012 --> 00:33:36,048
I'm not corpulent,
I'm big boned.

917
00:33:37,015 --> 00:33:39,150
Digger Smolkin says,
"Eatest mine dust."

918
00:33:39,183 --> 00:33:40,352
It seems like a nice night,

919
00:33:40,385 --> 00:33:42,755
but I do not know for I am mad.

920
00:33:43,788 --> 00:33:45,792
I call it Bowling
Ball in Repose.

921
00:33:49,327 --> 00:33:52,465
This movie's like
a medieval Ghost, huh?

922
00:33:52,498 --> 00:33:53,832
Thank you, Scroop.

923
00:33:53,865 --> 00:33:55,733
You can leave the
ale on the table.

924
00:33:55,767 --> 00:33:57,903
Has Adam come with the
chaps to prison quarters?

925
00:33:57,937 --> 00:34:00,138
So they had filthy
walls back then, too?

926
00:34:01,607 --> 00:34:02,742
No, I am not she.

927
00:34:03,775 --> 00:34:05,210
Forgive the look
on my face, Livia.

928
00:34:05,243 --> 00:34:06,578
I'm just butt-ugly.

929
00:34:06,612 --> 00:34:09,647
- For a moment, I-
- Be not ashamed of love.

930
00:34:09,680 --> 00:34:12,218
Please, I have to finish
my sculpture of Eisenhower.

931
00:34:13,752 --> 00:34:14,987
My thanks for
bringing the ale.

932
00:34:15,020 --> 00:34:16,388
That's a nice skort on.

933
00:34:16,422 --> 00:34:17,422
Your drink could
bring but only

934
00:34:17,455 --> 00:34:20,025
half the forgetfulness you seek.

935
00:34:20,058 --> 00:34:21,527
And what of the other half?

936
00:34:22,728 --> 00:34:23,830
Look to me for it.

937
00:34:25,330 --> 00:34:27,767
Mmm, her breath
smells like Fancy Feast.

938
00:34:29,868 --> 00:34:31,235
Ooh, you're tongue
is like sandpaper.

939
00:34:31,268 --> 00:34:32,703
I can only presume
that you have, by that,

940
00:34:32,737 --> 00:34:34,940
released some violence
that has inflamed thee.

941
00:34:34,973 --> 00:34:35,975
Speaking of inflamed...

942
00:34:36,008 --> 00:34:37,575
For years.

943
00:34:37,608 --> 00:34:39,912
I would not bring the truth
of it before thee now, if...

944
00:34:39,945 --> 00:34:41,313
Now-eth?
(group chuckles)

945
00:34:41,347 --> 00:34:44,082
If that Helene were
not as good as dead.

946
00:34:44,115 --> 00:34:45,850
As good as dead
is not dead, Livia.

947
00:34:45,883 --> 00:34:47,152
But she will be, let's rock.

948
00:34:47,185 --> 00:34:50,022
The first light of morning,
she will be lost to you.

949
00:34:50,055 --> 00:34:51,188
Wow, eager gal.

950
00:34:51,222 --> 00:34:52,457
Our spirits may
despair, Pendragon,

951
00:34:52,490 --> 00:34:55,493
but dare those spirits
tie the hands of flesh?

952
00:34:55,527 --> 00:34:58,797
- Do not tempt me.
- I do not tempt, I give.

953
00:34:58,830 --> 00:35:00,532
She's perky, I
like her attitude.

954
00:35:00,565 --> 00:35:05,403
(Mystery Science Theater
3000 theme music)

955
00:35:07,740 --> 00:35:08,807
Where have you brought me?

956
00:35:08,840 --> 00:35:10,475
The deepest
part of the forest.

957
00:35:10,508 --> 00:35:12,710
Go you through the brambles
till you see a light.

958
00:35:12,743 --> 00:35:14,813
There you will find
a house and hearth.

959
00:35:14,847 --> 00:35:15,948
A house?

960
00:35:15,982 --> 00:35:17,748
Will I be safe there?

961
00:35:17,782 --> 00:35:19,717
A madman can't
be sure of that.

962
00:35:19,750 --> 00:35:22,420
No more than whether you
bewitched me, or did not.

963
00:35:22,453 --> 00:35:24,388
Oh, sure, throw that at me.

964
00:35:24,422 --> 00:35:26,792
♪ Hey, diddle diddle,
the rat and the fiddle

965
00:35:26,825 --> 00:35:27,860
Oh...

966
00:35:27,893 --> 00:35:29,428
♪ The corpse jumped
over his tomb

967
00:35:29,462 --> 00:35:30,762
Now that's purely gratuitous.

968
00:35:30,795 --> 00:35:32,332
That stinks.
(frog croaks)

969
00:35:35,100 --> 00:35:37,803
That frog's a
good licking size.

970
00:35:37,837 --> 00:35:38,937
(Helene cries out)

971
00:35:38,970 --> 00:35:41,140
A small, amphibious
reptile, run!

972
00:35:42,107 --> 00:35:44,343
Hey, there's smudge
in the orange grove.

973
00:35:45,643 --> 00:35:46,712
Ah, it's noon.

974
00:35:46,745 --> 00:35:50,248
Corman's theory of
directing, light, and get away.

975
00:35:50,282 --> 00:35:52,017
Hey, that leather
mug salesman's

976
00:35:52,050 --> 00:35:53,818
doing all right for himself.

977
00:35:55,787 --> 00:35:57,190
What a pretty yamaka.

978
00:35:58,790 --> 00:36:01,827
Grumpy, Grump, Sneezy,
let me in, it's Snow!

979
00:36:03,795 --> 00:36:05,263
James Woods.
(Helene screams)

980
00:36:06,698 --> 00:36:08,667
- I don't like tudor houses!
- Enough of this.

981
00:36:08,700 --> 00:36:10,235
I demand you bring
her out of it, now.

982
00:36:10,268 --> 00:36:11,370
No, Professor...

983
00:36:11,403 --> 00:36:12,570
- Is he sitting on her?
- I don't know

984
00:36:12,603 --> 00:36:13,672
what's being done
to her, right now,

985
00:36:13,705 --> 00:36:15,340
but the shock of
returning might kill her.

986
00:36:15,373 --> 00:36:17,075
We may already
have done that.

987
00:36:17,108 --> 00:36:19,712
But enough of us,
back to our film.

988
00:36:19,745 --> 00:36:21,213
Come inside, my dear.

989
00:36:21,247 --> 00:36:23,315
Oh, it's the Olive Garden.

990
00:36:23,348 --> 00:36:24,950
Yeah, I also hate
it when they seat you

991
00:36:24,983 --> 00:36:26,285
before you get a
look at the menu.

992
00:36:26,318 --> 00:36:27,753
- Yeah.
- Ugh.

993
00:36:28,753 --> 00:36:30,788
So I bought land
on the edge of Mordor,

994
00:36:30,822 --> 00:36:31,657
it's really coming back.

995
00:36:31,690 --> 00:36:33,058
These are the
designs of the prison

996
00:36:33,092 --> 00:36:34,827
towers and passageways.

997
00:36:34,860 --> 00:36:35,962
Thank you, Plop.

998
00:36:37,662 --> 00:36:39,230
Well, I got a party
of eight coming in,

999
00:36:39,263 --> 00:36:40,833
jousting rush just started.

1000
00:36:43,635 --> 00:36:45,470
- Ah, and we're back.
- Wow.

1001
00:36:45,503 --> 00:36:47,940
There's still some
contact, her lips are moving.

1002
00:36:47,973 --> 00:36:49,642
Please get me
out of this film.

1003
00:36:49,675 --> 00:36:50,775
- But there's no speech.
- Please?

1004
00:36:50,808 --> 00:36:52,677
I'll go back to
waitressing, I promise.

1005
00:36:52,710 --> 00:36:55,313
She may be this way
until the end of her life.

1006
00:36:57,415 --> 00:37:00,185
- Which one?
- Witch one, get it?

1007
00:37:00,218 --> 00:37:01,687
- Witch one?
- Kill him.

1008
00:37:01,720 --> 00:37:04,723
(Crow laughs)
It's okay, it's okay.

1009
00:37:04,757 --> 00:37:06,858
- It's Corman. It's Corman.
- I know.

1010
00:37:06,892 --> 00:37:08,527
(Meg Maud cackles)

1011
00:37:08,560 --> 00:37:10,962
Tis a fine brew,
we are finished.

1012
00:37:10,995 --> 00:37:11,997
What will you do with me?

1013
00:37:12,030 --> 00:37:13,365
Who knows, my child?

1014
00:37:13,398 --> 00:37:14,967
Perhaps I'll turn
thee into an owl

1015
00:37:15,000 --> 00:37:16,902
to catch mice for my cauldron.

1016
00:37:16,935 --> 00:37:18,103
Then thou art a witch.

1017
00:37:18,137 --> 00:37:20,672
Find one who say Meg
Maud is not a witch.

1018
00:37:20,705 --> 00:37:23,408
And I'll turn
butter out of blood.

1019
00:37:23,442 --> 00:37:25,343
- Yuck.
- I know thee, Helene.

1020
00:37:25,377 --> 00:37:28,213
- Smolkin is my friend.
- Mother, please.

1021
00:37:28,247 --> 00:37:29,680
How did thou escape?

1022
00:37:29,713 --> 00:37:32,417
A voice that was mine
self in ages yet to come

1023
00:37:32,450 --> 00:37:34,252
did show me the way
to loose my bond.

1024
00:37:34,285 --> 00:37:36,588
- Ah!
- Ah, ah, ah.

1025
00:37:37,288 --> 00:37:38,290
By a voice?

1026
00:37:38,323 --> 00:37:40,892
In ages yet to come?

1027
00:37:40,925 --> 00:37:42,093
This is not the sort of magic

1028
00:37:42,127 --> 00:37:44,328
that Satan has given to me.

1029
00:37:44,362 --> 00:37:45,897
Then thou art a witch?

1030
00:37:45,930 --> 00:37:48,100
I was at thy trial.

1031
00:37:48,133 --> 00:37:50,202
I heard the witness Livia swear

1032
00:37:50,235 --> 00:37:54,205
that she did see thee
cast a spell on Smolkin.

1033
00:37:54,238 --> 00:37:56,675
So uh, how do
you like your eggs?

1034
00:37:56,708 --> 00:37:59,678
One last ingredient
for my brew.

1035
00:37:59,712 --> 00:38:00,712
Oh, yeah.

1036
00:38:00,745 --> 00:38:04,615
One raven strand
of maiden virtue.

1037
00:38:04,648 --> 00:38:06,985
It seems like David
Brinkley, "one raven strand"...

1038
00:38:07,018 --> 00:38:09,220
Thou does not
mean to kill me?

1039
00:38:09,253 --> 00:38:11,490
They have named thee witch.

1040
00:38:11,523 --> 00:38:13,458
If I am a witch,
the same as thee,

1041
00:38:13,492 --> 00:38:15,327
should not sister help sister?

1042
00:38:15,360 --> 00:38:16,528
Huh? I didn't get that.

1043
00:38:16,562 --> 00:38:19,030
Aye, aye, that is true.

1044
00:38:19,063 --> 00:38:20,665
We witches must stand together.

1045
00:38:20,698 --> 00:38:21,967
(Meg Maud laughs)

1046
00:38:22,000 --> 00:38:23,268
Good, well said, Helene.

1047
00:38:23,302 --> 00:38:25,503
Perhaps I'll give thee thy head.

1048
00:38:25,537 --> 00:38:27,172
Stay here, little witch,

1049
00:38:27,205 --> 00:38:29,975
and bar the door to all but me.

1050
00:38:31,208 --> 00:38:32,610
I'm going down
to the Winn-Dixie

1051
00:38:32,643 --> 00:38:34,647
for some grease that's sweating
from the murderer's pubic.

1052
00:38:34,680 --> 00:38:37,348
I have some conjouring to do.

1053
00:38:37,382 --> 00:38:39,150
Oh, could you pick
me up some Rice Dream?

1054
00:38:39,183 --> 00:38:41,787
- She's a weirdo, man.
- Mmhmm.

1055
00:38:46,658 --> 00:38:50,728
She's hitting happy hour
with Margaret Hamilton.

1056
00:38:50,762 --> 00:38:53,765
(knocks at door)
Community Theater Witch!

1057
00:38:55,200 --> 00:38:57,537
Must be here for
my Ox Stomach Pudding.

1058
00:39:00,138 --> 00:39:01,373
Now there's a
fine face to see

1059
00:39:01,407 --> 00:39:02,875
on such a fine night!

1060
00:39:02,908 --> 00:39:03,975
Let me in, Scroop.

1061
00:39:04,008 --> 00:39:05,712
You hiring strippers?

1062
00:39:06,345 --> 00:39:07,378
Who else has been here?

1063
00:39:07,412 --> 00:39:09,413
- Helene has escaped.
- Escaped?

1064
00:39:09,447 --> 00:39:10,548
- Escaped!
- Escaped.

1065
00:39:10,582 --> 00:39:11,750
Well, there've
been no soldiers.

1066
00:39:11,783 --> 00:39:14,587
Pendragon is upstairs,
with a maiden, Livia.

1067
00:39:14,620 --> 00:39:16,922
Livia?
Call him down.

1068
00:39:18,157 --> 00:39:19,992
Ho! Pendragon!
(group laughs)

1069
00:39:20,025 --> 00:39:21,125
I coulda done that, jeez!

1070
00:39:21,158 --> 00:39:23,962
Say nothing to Livia,
she must not learn of this.

1071
00:39:23,995 --> 00:39:25,763
Huzzah, who's the babe?

1072
00:39:25,797 --> 00:39:29,767
This is Meg Maud, she has
news of great import for thee.

1073
00:39:29,800 --> 00:39:32,003
Ask nothing, get
thee with all haste

1074
00:39:32,037 --> 00:39:32,437
to my cottage in the marsh.

1075
00:39:32,470 --> 00:39:34,105
And you are...

1076
00:39:34,138 --> 00:39:35,873
It's just beyond the hillock
where they hang the highwaymen.

1077
00:39:35,907 --> 00:39:37,308
What say thee?

1078
00:39:37,342 --> 00:39:39,945
Ask nothing, ride as
thou thy horse had wings!

1079
00:39:39,978 --> 00:39:41,447
I trust you implicitly.

1080
00:39:43,315 --> 00:39:45,050
Now I'll go play
with his clothes.

1081
00:39:46,685 --> 00:39:48,687
(cat meows)
(Crow hacks)

1082
00:39:49,587 --> 00:39:51,723
(knocking at door)
I'm shapeshifting.

1083
00:39:51,757 --> 00:39:54,092
The door's
unlatched, pray enter.

1084
00:39:54,125 --> 00:39:56,628
(group singsongs)

1085
00:39:57,830 --> 00:40:00,332
What be thy business
with Pendragon, witch?

1086
00:40:00,365 --> 00:40:02,602
I think that I
shall marry him.

1087
00:40:02,635 --> 00:40:03,202
Ha!

1088
00:40:03,235 --> 00:40:04,368
He would not have thee

1089
00:40:04,402 --> 00:40:06,805
with thy gullet
stuffed with gold.

1090
00:40:06,838 --> 00:40:09,307
- You called me "witch."
- That really hurt.

1091
00:40:09,340 --> 00:40:12,310
No woman, man, or
creature like yourself

1092
00:40:12,343 --> 00:40:13,512
has dared to call me that and--

1093
00:40:13,545 --> 00:40:16,013
Lived to see another, witch?

1094
00:40:16,047 --> 00:40:16,982
I wasn't gonna say that.

1095
00:40:17,015 --> 00:40:18,850
We know one the other well.

1096
00:40:18,883 --> 00:40:22,453
One day, thy mother
did bear a female child.

1097
00:40:22,487 --> 00:40:25,123
And on another day she
did sell her soul to Satan

1098
00:40:25,157 --> 00:40:26,692
and become his bird of prey.

1099
00:40:26,725 --> 00:40:27,892
Oh, so you know about that.

1100
00:40:27,925 --> 00:40:31,128
One day, my mother
bore a female child,

1101
00:40:31,162 --> 00:40:33,565
and she did grow
aged and deformed.

1102
00:40:33,598 --> 00:40:34,798
Is this blank verse?

1103
00:40:34,832 --> 00:40:37,735
And on another day,
she cheated Satan,

1104
00:40:37,768 --> 00:40:40,872
learned his tricks and
yet retained her soul.

1105
00:40:40,905 --> 00:40:41,607
And her water.

1106
00:40:41,640 --> 00:40:43,608
I am thy match, witch,

1107
00:40:43,642 --> 00:40:46,312
but I am not thy kind.

1108
00:40:46,345 --> 00:40:47,612
I know it well.

1109
00:40:47,645 --> 00:40:48,813
You're just mad
that Bobby Russell

1110
00:40:48,847 --> 00:40:51,448
didn't ask you to the ski trip.

1111
00:40:51,482 --> 00:40:54,518
You will make
me a fine opponent.

1112
00:40:54,552 --> 00:40:55,687
What the hell is this,

1113
00:40:55,720 --> 00:40:57,823
a bust of Chiang Kai-shek
made out of liver?

1114
00:40:59,392 --> 00:41:00,592
Ooh!

1115
00:41:01,358 --> 00:41:02,760
- Take care, strumpet!
- Gimme!

1116
00:41:02,793 --> 00:41:06,263
I know thy magic
better than thyself.

1117
00:41:06,297 --> 00:41:12,037
(Mystery Science Theater
3000 theme music)

1118
00:41:12,070 --> 00:41:14,540
Do you get free tailoring
on each suit you buy?

1119
00:41:14,573 --> 00:41:15,907
I guarantee it.

1120
00:41:15,940 --> 00:41:18,110
Is there water at the
bottom of the ocean?

1121
00:41:18,143 --> 00:41:20,012
I guarantee it.

1122
00:41:20,045 --> 00:41:21,078
Do I guarantee it?

1123
00:41:21,112 --> 00:41:22,813
I guarantee it.

1124
00:41:22,847 --> 00:41:24,582
Ah, Crow, you
wanna get going?

1125
00:41:24,615 --> 00:41:25,850
'Cause we're gonna get a
Hot Pocket or something.

1126
00:41:25,883 --> 00:41:27,852
I guar... Oh, sure, great.
Okay, great.

1127
00:41:27,885 --> 00:41:29,888
Fist full of
Philly Beef, for me.

1128
00:41:29,922 --> 00:41:30,688
Whoa!

1129
00:41:30,722 --> 00:41:32,557
Who hath summoned me?

1130
00:41:32,590 --> 00:41:34,258
Well, I, I don't
think that I did.

1131
00:41:34,292 --> 00:41:35,627
Did you guys?

1132
00:41:35,660 --> 00:41:36,795
- I don't think so.
- No, not that I recall.

1133
00:41:36,828 --> 00:41:38,363
Someone has brought me here

1134
00:41:38,397 --> 00:41:40,598
from the realm of the unknown,

1135
00:41:40,632 --> 00:41:42,233
and I intend to, uh oh...

1136
00:41:42,267 --> 00:41:43,835
- Uh oh.
- Whoa.

1137
00:41:45,537 --> 00:41:46,838
Didn't mean to do that.

1138
00:41:47,605 --> 00:41:48,640
Didn't mean to do that.

1139
00:41:48,673 --> 00:41:50,908
Because I have
terrible, dark powers,

1140
00:41:50,942 --> 00:41:52,043
- Sure you do.
- Which I intend to...

1141
00:41:52,077 --> 00:41:53,212
- Yeah.
- Oh, cripes!

1142
00:41:54,278 --> 00:41:56,013
- There you go again.
- What the?

1143
00:41:56,047 --> 00:41:56,882
Oh.

1144
00:41:57,715 --> 00:41:59,985
Oh, never been
a football before.

1145
00:42:00,018 --> 00:42:00,785
That was cool.

1146
00:42:00,818 --> 00:42:02,820
The heck is going on, here?

1147
00:42:02,853 --> 00:42:04,655
Uh, ma'am, do you
need a glass of water?

1148
00:42:04,688 --> 00:42:05,890
- Yeah.
- Yes, you know...

1149
00:42:05,923 --> 00:42:06,758
No, no, I...

1150
00:42:07,492 --> 00:42:09,527
I want your very souls, and I...

1151
00:42:09,560 --> 00:42:10,895
- Oh, wow.
- Oh, boy.

1152
00:42:10,928 --> 00:42:11,930
Oh, oh!

1153
00:42:14,967 --> 00:42:16,702
Oh, penguin? Wow.

1154
00:42:17,435 --> 00:42:18,837
- Trying my best...
- Yeah.

1155
00:42:18,870 --> 00:42:21,238
- Just a little bit rusty...
- Sure, it takes it outta ya.

1156
00:42:21,272 --> 00:42:24,008
- It's just, oh boy!
- Whoa!

1157
00:42:26,845 --> 00:42:27,580
Wah!

1158
00:42:28,380 --> 00:42:29,080
Yikes.

1159
00:42:29,615 --> 00:42:31,683
Uh, ma'am?

1160
00:42:31,717 --> 00:42:33,318
Uh, evil, soul-stealing ma'am?

1161
00:42:33,352 --> 00:42:35,787
Ah, shape-shifting
bride of Satan?

1162
00:42:35,820 --> 00:42:37,355
Uh, Missus Witchiness?

1163
00:42:37,388 --> 00:42:38,690
Oh, darn it.

1164
00:42:38,723 --> 00:42:41,258
I'm stuck, and, I'm stuck!

1165
00:42:41,292 --> 00:42:42,893
Oh, this is so annoying.

1166
00:42:42,927 --> 00:42:44,128
Well, whenever you get--
(klaxon buzzes)

1167
00:42:44,162 --> 00:42:45,497
Movie sign!

1168
00:42:45,530 --> 00:42:48,800
Hey, where are you going...
(voice recedes)

1169
00:42:50,068 --> 00:42:52,137
(chains rattle)

1170
00:42:52,170 --> 00:42:56,308
(gates clang)

1171
00:42:57,808 --> 00:42:59,243
You know, we could
use some bleach.

1172
00:42:59,277 --> 00:43:00,712
Still tonight, Helene.

1173
00:43:00,745 --> 00:43:02,547
Still one deadly night.

1174
00:43:02,580 --> 00:43:04,048
Let's have some soup.

1175
00:43:04,082 --> 00:43:04,617
Where's Meg?

1176
00:43:04,650 --> 00:43:05,283
The witch?

1177
00:43:05,317 --> 00:43:06,318
She's at the bar.

1178
00:43:06,352 --> 00:43:08,420
For she thinks I
am the same as she.

1179
00:43:08,453 --> 00:43:10,020
I fooled her.
(Pendragon laughs)

1180
00:43:10,053 --> 00:43:12,257
You couldn't fool
a child in his cradle.

1181
00:43:12,290 --> 00:43:13,492
Gee, thanks.

1182
00:43:13,525 --> 00:43:14,758
She is the one sent
me here to find you.

1183
00:43:14,792 --> 00:43:16,127
Why'd you ask where she is?

1184
00:43:16,160 --> 00:43:17,728
I'm glad of that.

1185
00:43:17,762 --> 00:43:20,465
And yet, Pendragon, this
place, 'tis unhealthy.

1186
00:43:20,498 --> 00:43:21,698
I sense radon.

1187
00:43:21,732 --> 00:43:24,770
Well come, then, I'll
take you to the tavern.

1188
00:43:24,803 --> 00:43:26,705
Scroop is a good fellow.

1189
00:43:26,738 --> 00:43:29,240
He'll help watch
over you, come on.

1190
00:43:29,273 --> 00:43:31,442
We'll get a burger basket
and a couple of lineys.

1191
00:43:31,475 --> 00:43:35,813
So, you would
enchant Pendragon as
you did poor Smolkin.

1192
00:43:35,847 --> 00:43:37,915
We shall see, my dear.

1193
00:43:37,948 --> 00:43:39,450
So we shall.

1194
00:43:39,483 --> 00:43:41,553
Helene lives but
a few more hours.

1195
00:43:41,587 --> 00:43:43,253
Then Pendragon is mine.

1196
00:43:43,287 --> 00:43:46,023
- I’ll take that challenge.
- And your little dog, too.

1197
00:43:46,057 --> 00:43:46,625
Hark you this:

1198
00:43:47,592 --> 00:43:49,727
Pendragon shall be
free of thee forever.

1199
00:43:49,760 --> 00:43:52,497
And what's more,
the maid condemed

1200
00:43:52,530 --> 00:43:53,965
shall live beyond this night,

1201
00:43:53,998 --> 00:43:56,902
and live to see
thee to thy death.

1202
00:43:56,935 --> 00:43:58,035
Says you!

1203
00:43:58,068 --> 00:44:01,272
Is it a wager, then, my
twisted copy of a wizardess?

1204
00:44:01,305 --> 00:44:04,808
Try every trick you
know, I'll vanquish thee.

1205
00:44:04,842 --> 00:44:06,845
And I'll do it in my sleep.

1206
00:44:06,878 --> 00:44:08,313
- You got me.
- Sleep?

1207
00:44:08,347 --> 00:44:10,115
Not while I'm awake.

1208
00:44:10,915 --> 00:44:13,052
Aye, sleep is coming.

1209
00:44:13,685 --> 00:44:15,787
In the sulphurous pit!

1210
00:44:15,820 --> 00:44:17,788
You mean Scroop's underarm?

1211
00:44:17,822 --> 00:44:19,223
Oh, she's good,
she nailed me there.

1212
00:44:19,257 --> 00:44:21,160
Whew. Zing.

1213
00:44:24,628 --> 00:44:26,932
Now I understand
dwarf-tossing.

1214
00:44:27,832 --> 00:44:29,902
Good, old fashioned
nightmare fuel.

1215
00:44:31,702 --> 00:44:34,205
You know, this forest
could use a plant.

1216
00:44:35,940 --> 00:44:38,777
This kingdom has
maybe six people.

1217
00:44:40,745 --> 00:44:43,382
♪ Me in White Satin
(Mike chuckles)

1218
00:44:43,415 --> 00:44:44,717
Sorry.

1219
00:44:45,717 --> 00:44:47,987
There goes the dumbest
knight in the realm.

1220
00:44:50,153 --> 00:44:52,157
Let us now fly to
Smolkin's church yard,

1221
00:44:52,190 --> 00:44:53,692
and there prepare
the tables of earth

1222
00:44:53,725 --> 00:44:55,393
for the banquet of the Sabbath.

1223
00:44:56,493 --> 00:44:58,530
Let us be little B-1 Bombers.

1224
00:44:58,563 --> 00:45:00,432
(Smokin sings)
Ah, jeez.

1225
00:45:00,465 --> 00:45:02,233
- Oh, man.
- Do you have a gun?

1226
00:45:04,568 --> 00:45:05,903
(Crow imitates Smolkin singing)

1227
00:45:05,937 --> 00:45:09,673
♪ She tried, but the
corpse sadly cried

1228
00:45:09,707 --> 00:45:10,842
Reconnaissance!

1229
00:45:10,875 --> 00:45:13,378
Be off, ghoul,
and leave me alone.

1230
00:45:13,412 --> 00:45:15,013
The first highway worker.

1231
00:45:15,913 --> 00:45:17,248
Good evening, Smolkin.

1232
00:45:17,282 --> 00:45:18,417
From a Sara!

1233
00:45:18,450 --> 00:45:20,352
Ah, 'tis Livia, the witch.

1234
00:45:20,385 --> 00:45:22,720
Welcome to my flesh farm.

1235
00:45:22,753 --> 00:45:24,422
Disturb me not, lummox.

1236
00:45:24,455 --> 00:45:26,423
I must hasten to sweep
these wandering ghosts back

1237
00:45:26,457 --> 00:45:29,127
to their earthen homes before
the witch's Sabbath begins.

1238
00:45:29,160 --> 00:45:31,930
Oh, and are you to
be the Queen of Sorcery

1239
00:45:31,963 --> 00:45:33,665
at the revelry tonight, Livia?

1240
00:45:33,698 --> 00:45:36,133
Aye, and stand at
Lucifer's right hand.

1241
00:45:36,167 --> 00:45:37,768
- Cool.
- ’Tis said the queen

1242
00:45:37,802 --> 00:45:40,805
must bring to Satan's hand
one freshly severed head

1243
00:45:40,838 --> 00:45:43,808
as proof that she is
true to his black trust.

1244
00:45:43,842 --> 00:45:46,712
A head. I never got...

1245
00:45:46,745 --> 00:45:47,945
- Take Smolkins'!
- Yeah!

1246
00:45:47,978 --> 00:45:49,180
- Get him, get his head!
- Say I cut yours off?

1247
00:45:49,213 --> 00:45:50,482
- The head of a madman,
- Yeah, let's do it!

1248
00:45:50,515 --> 00:45:52,017
Yes, yes, yes, yes.

1249
00:45:52,817 --> 00:45:53,885
The devil might feel slighted

1250
00:45:53,918 --> 00:45:55,753
if you brought him
less than the best.

1251
00:45:55,787 --> 00:45:56,922
He's not that picky.

1252
00:45:56,955 --> 00:45:59,823
Pity, thou must
seek elsewhere.

1253
00:45:59,857 --> 00:46:02,827
I must hurry home to
see how fare my charges.

1254
00:46:02,860 --> 00:46:04,997
He's violating
a lot of fire laws.

1255
00:46:06,730 --> 00:46:09,167
They mustn't
know of our love.

1256
00:46:09,200 --> 00:46:11,637
I have the urge to pour
Frangelico out of his neck.

1257
00:46:11,670 --> 00:46:12,703
Me too.

1258
00:46:12,737 --> 00:46:13,838
You should not
have brought her here!

1259
00:46:13,872 --> 00:46:15,907
The night is filled
with soldiers.

1260
00:46:15,940 --> 00:46:17,875
We saw them,
it is safer here.

1261
